#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a441dca-25da-57b4-b90c-27dfb3b87a19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{105.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299813} {:answer/id #uuid "13964d5a-9967-5ef6-9b12-d693f54cae14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{123.2}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299814} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ae7195-cfbc-5e22-944d-afe431f5cdca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299815} {:answer/id #uuid "bda0f309-e6e5-5017-8ce0-b80ffba45cd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{95.9}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299816} {:answer/id #uuid "86e52145-75b1-5720-bbb3-99b6a2e78b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{115.2}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a441dca-25da-57b4-b90c-27dfb3b87a19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{105.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299813} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f7c4f24-38ef-52a3-a79c-0c6c63b4ef63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47778997-e90f-5f7d-b2f9-574ccbc3b4d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-125078" :question/problem "Given that $a\\cdot b=-9$, find the angle between $a=⟨-2t,3t⟩$ and $b=⟨3,1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $a\\cdot b=-9$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-9 \\\\ -2t\\cdot 3+3t\\cdot 1 & =-9 \\\\ -6t+3t & =-9 \\\\ -3t & =-9 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨-2(3),\\,3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{9}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{117}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{3\\sqrt{13}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{130}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{130}})≈{105.3}^{∘}.\n$$"}]}
